cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Seismic Fractal Analysis: Multi-Planar Hierarchy Framework"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025-12-08
abstract: |
  Python framework for fractal dimension analysis of earthquake spatial distributions.
  Implements Grassberger-Procaccia correlation dimension estimation, Rényi multifractal
  spectrum analysis, topological graph structure detection via Leiden clustering, and
  bootstrap uncertainty quantification. Includes Bayesian methods for observational bias
  correction and adaptive parameter selection. Designed for analyzing large seismic catalogs
  (N>5,000 events) with consumer hardware accessibility. Three-tier deployment: web app,
  Colab notebook, and Python package.

